hi there I'm Anna Prosser Robinson for  GameSpot here at the Ubisoft booth at e3  2014 I'm standing here with Andrew who  is a game developer for Ubisoft and Jen  who does community development who's  also a great friend of mine which is  exciting and we're here to talk about  Rainbow six siege I just got to watch  the live demo which was pretty  impressive  now as a game developer when you take on  something like Tom Clancy's Rainbow six  what goes into deciding what you're  gonna do for a new game while still  staying true to what people love about a  series for us it was always about  getting back to the basics of the  franchise really really going back and  exploring what makes Rainbow six Rainbow  six now what made the the father a  tactical shooter is you know what what's  what's the beating heart of the  franchise and for us we iterated for a  while and we went back to the basics and  we actually came to this brand new  asymmetrical gameplay which we call a  siege gameplay all about the attackers  versus the defenders the attackers the  Masters of destruction these guys are  all our destruction experts right they  place breach charges make new paths the  defenders know that the attack is coming  the assault is coming and they're all  about fortifying on the objective  preparing for the assault and we lose  saw this and we saw this game play and  we really we stress it to the nth degree  and we incorporated a brand new  procedural destruction system to give  creativity to both sides and this is the  been the backbone of developing Rainbow  six siege there has been a lot of  destruction that I've seen in this game  it looks like part of the fun is just  blowing up like a suburban house right  well yeah it's the son of the experience  and it's the center with player  creativity on both sides attack in  defense  the attackers can place breach charges  on on walls and floors and make new  navigational opportunities get the drop  on on the on their enemies on the  defenders side you actually take a shot  they usually take shotguns that they can  ambush enemies by blowing a hole through  a wall and everything breaks based on  the material it is so when you take a  shotgun you blow a gypsy wall it's gonna  break just like jibs and like throwing a  c4 the other side and getting the drop  in ambushing and trapping some people  it's been really fun and players are  really playing with it and doing new  things that we didn't even think like oh  my god that was the best play ever so  it's been really fun and yeah the  destruction is really really cool in  Rainbow six siege it strikes me as kind  of that Second Life that all gamers want  to have like you know you're looking at  your house and I could throw a bomb at  that wall  you know renovation exactly so you know  that you said that the decision was made  to really focus on multiplayer here why  was that so important for this game in  particular well multiplayer has always  been a really strong part of the rainbow  franchise and as we were to making it we  wanted to put the the player experience  for first in the game with multiplayer  and really kind of you know iterate on  that so that's why I'm the siege  gameplay worked really well because you  need you know attack and defense and  that asymmetry and again we we iterated  on it and we it was so much fun so we  just we have a pre-alpha build right now  and the multiplayer game mode it's a 5v5  hostage-rescue it with no respawn we've  been we've been testing and playing it  internally and it's been so much fun so  we just wanted to you show the world  what we have and that's you know we're  doing at e3 so we wanted to put the  multiplayer experience cuz it's been so  fun so far we focused on that first  well we talked to a lot of game  developers here at e3 but tell the  viewers at home what a community  developer does for a game but a  community tough developer does for a  game well I've been working since the  start for a year and a half with the  team making sure to build the proper  platform and tool so that the community  when they're ready they can hop on board  and have a lot of fun together and grow  into something really amazing and until  that what I have right now on the team  is my community basically the dev team  is the community so we've been running  like you play a lot together we've run  internal tournaments and it's so much  fun and it's so great when you win with  your team you get up and you're like  buddies are right there you're high-five  it's really fun and I think the  community will be able to do that  someday  coming into a multiplayer game  especially it's going to be really  important to have a vibrant community  for a game how do you see that  developing for Rainbow six what do you  think people can expect to find in terms  of the groups of people they're going to  be playing with well I feel like this is  an interesting question it was a long  and drawn-out question I'm sorry yeah  well I hope that a lot of communities  are going to be able to gather around  Rainbow six siege like I think that a  lot of FPS fans are going to be able to  find something for them there but also  tactical fans I think that even RTS fans  might be interested in this there's so  much strategy that goes into it so much  planning like we sit down we look at the  maps we make plans we draw like  between games we even like do like we  talk about the games without the game  being there it's a lot of fun it's  really cool well being that I talked to  you quite frequently I know that you  know this is something you've been  working on for a long time you mentioned  you've been working on it for a long  time as well at e3 you finally got to  kind of announce what you've been  working on and tell everyone what you  secretly couldn't tell them before how  does that feel to finally announce this  project you've been working on so long  it feels amazing like when we were  waiting for the video to go on the stage  I was just in my ship my chair for some  reason I was nervous as the video could  crash and there was no way it would  happen it was like oh my god oh my god  it was really really good and feels  great to be able to like tweet about it  and have people respond and everyone  everyone has been so positive so far  it's amazing and what do you hope people  are going to do as they start to receive  and take this in and look forward to  beyond this pre alpha stage Oh  moving forward really focusing on the  C's receives gameplay and stressing it  even more again we're pre alpha right  now as we continue to iterate on the  game and push forward on different modes  and different things were going to be  doing we have a lot of top-secret things  we have waiting in stores for fans so  we're looking forward to showing it  sharing more in the future what we have  in store great thanks so much for your  time guys I really appreciate it  let me know what you think of Rainbow  six by tweeting at Anna Prosser with the  hashtag game spot III  you
 

